---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'AML Review Engine Lab';
const description = 'A Bionic Banker control-layer demo for blockchain AML triage: rules, anomaly signals, evidence records, human review, and clear limits.';

const metrics = [
  ['Local verification', '46 tests passing'],
  ['Detection claim in repo', '94.9% overall detection rate'],
  ['Rules documented', '28 rules'],
  ['Analyst queue reduction', '63% triage reduction'],
];

const flow = [
  ['1. Input', 'Wallet or transaction activity enters the review lane.'],
  ['2. Rules', 'Known patterns flag threshold, velocity, sanctions, mixer, bridge, phishing, or structuring signals.'],
  ['3. Anomaly layer', 'Isolation Forest-style anomaly detection adds a second view for unusual graph behavior.'],
  ['4. Triage', 'Signals become priority labels so human review focuses on the highest-value cases.'],
  ['5. Evidence note', 'The output must explain what was seen, what sources support it, and what remains uncertain.'],
  ['6. Human boundary', 'The system informs review. It does not approve, file, freeze, trade, or accuse.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://bionicbanker.tech/labs/aml-engine/">
  <main class="page-wrap">
    <section class="hero-section compact">
      <p class="eyebrow">Bionic Lab 01</p>
      <h1>AML Review Engine Lab</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical blockchain AML triage demo. The useful part is not only the score — it is the
        control layer around the score: rules, anomaly signals, evidence notes, triage labels, and review limits.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/labs/aml-engine/demo/">Open dashboard demo</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="/downloads/aml-demo-pack/aml-demo-pack-summary.pdf">Download demo summary</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="/downloads/aml-demo-pack/README.md">Open demo pack README</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/hash02/aml-detection-engine">View repository</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="/risk-evidence/">Risk evidence hub</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel-card" aria-label="AML control map">
      <p class="card-label">Visual proof</p>
      <h2>Control map</h2>
      <p>The lab is framed around a reviewable trail, not a black-box risk score.</p>
      <img class="lab-visual" src="/blog-visuals/aml-engine-lab/aml-control-map.png" alt="AML Review Engine control map showing wallet activity, rules, anomaly layer, triage, evidence note, and human review" loading="eager" />
    </section>

    <section class="content-grid two-up" aria-label="AML lab metrics">
      {metrics.map(([label, value]) => (
        <article class="panel-card">
          <p class="card-label">{label}</p>
          <h2>{value}</h2>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="panel-card" aria-label="What this proves">
      <p class="card-label">Control layer</p>
      <h2>What this lab proves</h2>
      <p>
        The lab shows how a crypto-risk workflow can move from raw activity to a reviewable record.
        It separates detection from decision, which is the core Bionic Banker principle: software can surface
        risk, but a human-controlled process owns the final interpretation and next action.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel-card" aria-label="AML review flow">
      <p class="card-label">Review flow</p>
      <h2>From wallet activity to review queue</h2>
      <div class="content-grid two-up">
        {flow.map(([step, text]) => (
          <article class="panel-card">
            <p class="card-label">{step}</p>
            <p>{text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel-card" aria-label="Verification record">
      <p class="card-label">Verification</p>
      <h2>Latest local check</h2>
      <p>The Wukong local copy was tested before this page was created.</p>
      <pre><code>cd /home/hash/aml-detection-engine
python3 -m pytest -q
..............................................                           [100%]</code></pre>
      <p>
        The local repository is currently behind its GitHub remote and has uncommitted changes, so the next
        engineering step is to reconcile the repo before publishing a packaged release.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel-card" aria-label="Limitations">
      <p class="card-label">Limits</p>
      <h2>What this lab does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It does not provide legal, regulatory, tax, compliance, trading, or investment advice.</li>
        <li>It does not identify a private actor behind an address without off-chain evidence.</li>
        <li>It does not freeze funds, file reports, approve KYC, or take enforcement action.</li>
        <li>It does not claim that every suspicious pattern is illicit activity.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-grid two-up" aria-label="Related Bionic records">
      <article class="panel-card">
        <p class="card-label">Related</p>
        <h2>Wallet risk notes</h2>
        <p>Read the public wallet-risk explanation and how risk rows should be interpreted.</p>
        <a href="/wallet-risk/">Open wallet risk →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="panel-card">
        <p class="card-label">Next</p>
        <h2>Package the demo</h2>
        <p>The next step is a sanitized demo bundle: sample input, sample output, risk memo, and visual control map.</p>
        <a href="/labs/">Back to Labs →</a>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
  <style is:global>
    .page-wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
    .hero-section { border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.35); border-radius: 28px; padding: 3rem; background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 0%, rgba(31,160,104,.18), transparent 42%), rgba(2,10,6,.72); box-shadow: 0 0 50px rgba(31,160,104,.08); }
    .eyebrow, .card-label { color: #7ee0aa; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .16em; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.8rem); line-height: .94; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -.055em; }
    .lede { max-width: 870px; color: #d7eee0; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.55; }
    .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: .9rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .panel-card { border: 1px solid rgba(138,138,160,.28); border-radius: 22px; padding: 1.35rem; background: rgba(3,13,8,.72); }
    .panel-card h2 { margin: 0 0 .8rem; font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); }
    .panel-card p, .panel-card li { color: #dceee3; line-height: 1.65; }
    .panel-card a { color: #7ee0aa; font-weight: 800; }
    .lab-visual { width: 100%; border-radius: 18px; border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.28); margin-top: 1rem; }
    .content-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
    .two-up { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    pre { background: #020604; border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.35); border-radius: 16px; padding: 1rem; overflow: auto; color: #e4e4ec; }
    section + section { margin-top: 1rem; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .two-up { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .hero-section { padding: 2rem; } }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
